{
 "schema": "pebble-sample-kit/1",
 "about": "The CC0 instrument samples that tools/audio/render_sampled.py plays the composed score with. Every file is fetched from the library's GitHub repository at the pinned commit by tools/audio/sample_kit.py (sample files and licence texts only; nothing downloaded is executed) into .work/audio/samples/<library>/<path> (gitignored), and verified against the git blob SHA-1 of the pinned tree and the SHA-256 recorded here. Only the samples the score plays are kept: every played pitch is within 3 semitones of a sampled one, and the layers, round robins and notes this score never reaches were pruned after the final render. Audio never enters git. A file's onset_ms, where present, overrides render_sampled.py's onset detection for that take.",
 "naming": "Both libraries name notes with middle C = C3 (Yamaha convention): a file named D4 sounds D5 (587 Hz). Measured on every pitched file by render_sampled.py, which tunes each note from the measured pitch.",
